+++ b/v6/sprefa-store/EXPERIMENT-G10-GOLDEN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+# G10 — golden-data bench: impl-level tracing + 1GB cache_size sweep, raw→sqlite→aggregate
+
+You own `v6/sprefa-store/` (code) and may WRITE data artifacts to `v6/labs/`
+(perf-runs.sqlite/.csv). Do not edit other crates or v6/labs source.
+
+## THE SPEC is `v6/labs/AGENTS.md` — read it first, implement it exactly.
+It defines the golden data every run must capture, the ~1GB reality, the
+cache_size question, the raw-sqlite-then-aggregate storage rule, and the sweep.
+This brief adds the ONE thing AGENTS.md leaves open: HOW the data is captured.
+
+## Capture via IMPL-LEVEL tracing (standard `tracing`, not trait-boundary)
+
+The user wants microscopes/sensors INSIDE the implementations, using standard
+tracing techniques — the project's tracing spine (standing law: telemetry rides
+`tracing`, never a bespoke pipeline). So:
+
+- Instrument the retract IMPLS in `src/cascade.rs` — `retract`, `retract_scc`,
+  `retract_dred` — with `tracing` spans and events at these granularities ONLY
+  (never per-row — a per-row span is the N+1 trap and perturbs timing):
+  - a top span per call: `#[instrument(skip_all, fields(engine, nodes, edges))]`
+    or `info_span!("retract", ...)`.
+  - a span per PHASE (build/insert/retract already separate; add per-phase spans).
+  - a span per fixpoint ROUND: `info_span!("round", n, frontier_rows)` (rounds =
+    graph depth, a few dozen — cheap).
+  - an event per DML: `info!(target:"bench::dml", stmt_idx, sql_prefix, rows_affected)`.
+  - events carrying the sensor deltas per round: sqlite cache hit/miss/write
+    delta, rows touched, ms.
+  - Replace the grandfathered `DL_CASCADE_TRACE` eprintln path with these tracing
+    events (keep the same information; route through tracing). No new eprintln.
+
+- In the bench harness, install a `tracing_subscriber::Layer` that materializes
+  span enter/exit timing + event fields into the raw store. This layer IS the
+  sensor readout — spans give you per-round/per-phase timing for free, events
+  give you the per-DML plan/rows. One process per cell still holds.
+
+## Sensors to wire (per AGENTS.md, via the layer + direct probes)
+- input_rust_bytes: `graph.rows.capacity()*size_of::<(u32,i64,i64)>()` +
+  `graph.edges.capacity()*size_of::<(u32,i64,u32,i64)>()` + adjacency map; also
+  RSS at end of build.
+- per-phase RSS (build/insert/retract) + rust_peak (memcap) + sqlite_hw.
+- RAM time-series: a sidecar thread sampling RSS+rust every ~50ms during retract.
+- disk read/write: macOS `rusage_info(RUSAGE_INFO_V2+)` `ri_diskio_bytesread/
+  written` via libc (NOT ru_inblock — 0 on Darwin); record source used.
+- sqlite cache hit/miss/write: `sqlite3_db_status(DBSTATUS_CACHE_HIT/MISS/WRITE)`
+  before+after retract (the direct readout of the cache_size knob).
+- EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN of every retract DML → query_plans table.
+- throughput = rows_retracted / t_retract_s.
+
+## Raw storage (source of truth) then aggregate
+- Append every run to `v6/labs/perf-runs.sqlite`: tables `runs` (one row/cell,
+  all scalar columns from AGENTS.md), `ram_timeseries(run_id,t_ms,rss_kb,rust_kb)`,
+  `query_plans(run_id,dml_index,sql_prefix,plan_text)`, `spans(run_id,name,n,
+  parent,enter_ms,dur_ms,fields_json)`, `events(run_id,target,ts_ms,fields_json)`.
+  Also export `runs` to `v6/labs/perf-runs.csv`. Never overwrite; append with a
+  `sweep_ts`.
+- Aggregation: extend the `gen-perf-charts.sh` pipeline (or a sibling) to read
+  `perf-runs.sqlite` and emit markdown tables + charts. The KEY chart: for each
+  engine, RSS and disk_write vs cache_size at fixed scale, and speed vs
+  cache_size — the knob trade curve. Markdown/charts are derived + disposable;
+  the sqlite/csv is the archive.
+
+## The sweep (per AGENTS.md)
+engine ∈ {sqlite-count, sqlite-count-scc, dd} × workload ∈ {DAG, CYC} × nodes
+∈ {a ladder} × cache_size ∈ {2000, 8000, 32000, 128000 KiB}, all under
+`DL_MEMCAP_MB=1024`, and a second pass at 512 to find the wall. dd is expected to
+ABORT under 1GB at higher scales — record `aborted=1, abort_phase`, do not treat
+as error. Keep the scale ladder modest enough that the WHOLE sweep finishes in a
+few minutes at first; correctness before coverage.
+
+## DISCIPLINE (hard)
+- Interpret numbers firsthand and DOUBT them; re-run headline cells; identical-
+  across-scale/cache_size numbers are a red flag to disprove.
+- Tracing must NOT perturb the measurement: span granularity is phase/round/DML,
+  never per-row. Verify overhead is negligible (compare a traced vs untraced
+  retract time once, report the delta).
+- Correctness = blake3 vs `benchgraph::oracle_survivors`. Never fabricate a
+  number or a query plan.
+- No new `eprintln!` in src/** (tracing only).
+
+## Validate
+- `cargo build` + `cargo test -p sprefa-store` green (agreement still passes).
+- The sweep populates `v6/labs/perf-runs.sqlite` (query it: `SELECT engine,
+  nodes, cache_size_kb, t_retract_ms, rss_retract_kb, cache_miss, disk_write_bytes
+  FROM runs LIMIT 20`) and `.csv`.
+- The aggregate chart shows the cache_size→{RSS, disk_write, speed} trade.
+
+## Commit
+Leave changes STAGED (`git add -A v6/sprefa-store v6/labs`). Do NOT commit
+(pre-commit hook needs `dl`). Coordinator commits.
+
+## Result file
+`v6/sprefa-store/EXPERIMENT-G10-RESULT.md`: the knob trade table (cache_size →
+speed/RSS/disk_write per engine at 1GB), your firsthand read, the traced-vs-
+untraced overhead delta, and the honest verdict on the smallest cache_size that
+finishes each scale under 1GB.
